cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: BioDynaX.jl
abstract: >-
  BioDynaX.jl fits hybrid models of small biochemical networks in Julia:
  known kinetics on a known interaction graph are compiled into a
  production-destruction ODE, one unknown destruction term is learned by a
  neural network trained on time-series data, and that term is then
  approximated symbolically by sparse rational regression over a library
  built from the node's graph neighbours.
authors:
